# TouchPoint Special Content

These Python scripts run as TouchPoint Special Content / PyScriptForm code.

## SQL is read-only

- Special Content may use **read-only** SQL only (`q.QuerySql`, `q.QuerySqlTop1`, SELECT).
- Do **not** use `model.ExecuteSql` or any INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE SQL. Writes fail (often as a generic `System.Exception`).
- Persist changes through TouchPoint model/API helpers instead, for example:
  - `model.WriteContentHtml` / `model.WriteContentPython` / `model.WriteContentText`
  - `model.SetSetting`
  - `model.AddOrganization`
  - Browser or `model.RestGet` / `model.RestPostJson` calls to official endpoints (e.g. `/api/v1/Involvements/{id}/Registrations/Settings` for `regShellId`)

## PyScriptForm rendering

- `model.Form`, `model.Styles`, and `model.Script` are for **GET** page loads.
- Full-page form POSTs will not paint `model.Form` (blank page). Use GET navigation and/or AJAX POST that returns JSON/`print` output, then navigate with GET.
- Wrap CSS in `<style>` tags when assigning `model.Styles`.

## User-facing copy

- Installer help text, notices, and labels should stay user-facing. Do **not** expose database column names, type IDs, SQL filters, setting key names, or other storage internals (e.g. `RegistrationTypeId = 26`).
- Exception: Shell Editor field/selector help may mention CSS selectors and similar coding details, because that helps people who edit shells manually.
